waila.item.panascais_caves:the_deep_mistake_scroll=Pergamena del profondo errore\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7They tunneled where no dwarf dared before.\nThe pick struck stone, but the stone bled\nblack. The mountain trembled and this was\nthe first breath "IT" took in millennia.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_binding_scroll=Pergamena del vincolo\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Five mages stood beneath the mountain's\nheart, hands trembling with grief. What\nthey forged was not art, but\nwarding-sigils drawn from pain, hammered\ninto silence.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_scattering_scroll=Pergamena della dispersione\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7One beast, five wards. To keep it\ndreaming, the sigils were shattered and\nburied in places no map names-where frost\ngnaws, fires weep, and nothing speaks.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_glyphs_scroll=Pergamena dei glifi\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7A stone altar listens beneath the world.\nFive marks wait-not for touch, but memory.\nThe matching must be true, or the silence\ndeepens.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_awakening_scroll=Pergamena del risveglio\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Pietra cracks. Dust breathes. The altar\ngroans beneath ancient weight. When the\nfifth mark finds its place, The Serpent\nstirs. Coils unwind, eyes open without\nlight, and the mountain forgets its\nsilence.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_trial_of_flame_scroll=Pergamena della prova della fiamma\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7In the lakes that blaze and howl, Ember\nwaits behind walls of living fire. Only\nthe worthy walk unscorched-their path\ncools where others burn.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_trial_of_water_scroll=Pergamena della prova dell'acqua\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Water hides where ice breathes blue and\nlight bends twice. Align the mirrors to\nreveal its shape-only perfect stillness\nsees what's real.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_trial_of_wind_scroll=Pergamena della prova del vento\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Wind drifts among open roots and quiet\nrivers. It does not lie still- follow the\nbreeze, and step where silence welcomes\nyou.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_trial_of_earth_scroll=Pergamena della prova della terra\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Buried in the earth, beneath dust and\ngemlight. Ametista spires and broken\ndeserts hold its shape. Only the\nheavy-hearted may lift it.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:whispers_of_the_forgemaster_scroll=Pergamena dei sussurri del maestro forgiatore\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7It cleaves stone, splits timber, and\ncarves paths no other tool dares-\nRunebreaker, the Forgiamaster's last\ncreation. Not forged to fight, but to\nshape the world itself. The runes bend to\nits will. The mountain remembers its name.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:lost_in_collapse_scroll=Pergamena perduta nel crollo\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7When the serpent was sealed away and the\nmountains fell silent, all records of the\nRunebreaker vanished. Some say it lies\nburied beneath the beast itself in the\nshattered altar, waiting for a soul bold\nenough to dig deep.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:facets_of_power_scroll=Pergamena delle sfaccettature del potere\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Six gemstones-Zaffiro, Sfalerite,\nSmeraldo, Rubino, Opale cristallino, and Onice-\neach forged as a fragment of dwarven\nmastery. Only when gathered can the\nancient tool be touched.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:runes_in_stone_scroll=Pergamena delle rune nella pietra\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7The serpent bears five wounds hidden\nbeneath petrified coil. When it falls,\nthey open... and the gemstones call out.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_forgotten_trial_scroll=Pergamena della prova dimenticata\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Nel boschetto dimenticato dal tempo, le\nrune dormono sotto reliquie sgretolate.\nCiò che il mondo dimentica, il tempo lo\nattende paziente per chi vuole cercare\nciò che è andato perduto.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_runebreaker_scroll=Pergamena del Runebreaker\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Inserisci le sei gemme in ciò che il\nserpente nasconde, e la montagna\nrisponderà. La reliquia si desterà. Non\ncon fiamma o acciaio, ma con un potere\na lungo negato.\n§r§r
